.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/.last-lint-result
observability/.state/

# Next.js / node
node_modules/
.next/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Mutation testing. `.stryker-tmp/` is the sandbox Stryker mutates inside — a
# full copy of the tree, so it must never be committed and must never be the
# thing anyone edits. `reports/` holds the run output; the baseline that matters
# lives in the pull request, not in git.
#
# Both anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored they would match a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, so a future `app/reports/` route would be silently
# untracked and fail only in CI on a clean clone — the same failure this file
# warns about for fixtures at the bottom.
/.stryker-tmp/
/reports/

# SLUICE_CONFIG_DIR lives here for local dev — never committed, same reason
# sluice.toml itself never is: it's a path into the household's own machine.
.env*.local

# Bank exports and household config never live here — they live outside the
# working tree entirely (see README). These patterns are a second line of
# defence, not the mechanism.
*.ofx
*.qif
*.csv
*.xlsx
sluice.toml

# ...with one deliberate exception. Fixtures are built in code rather than stored
# as files, so nothing here is currently excluded by the patterns above — this
# guards the day someone adds a stored synthetic export, which would otherwise be
# ignored silently and fail only in CI, on a clean clone, for no visible reason.
# Anything real is still rejected by the patterns above before reaching a commit.
!src/**/__fixtures__/**
